{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.IdealTetLawOfSines","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.IdealTetLawOfSines","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerLobachevsky"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.IdealTet.log_sin_sub_log_sin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.IdealTet.log_sin_sub_log_sin","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/IdealTetLawOfSines.lean#L136-L150","doc":"**The log form**, which is the shape the Λ-derivative produces:\n`log(2 sin θ₃) − log(2 sin θ₂) = −log ‖z‖`.\n\nThis is precisely the identity that makes the two sides of Kummer agree along a\nray, so it is worth having stated separately. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.IdealTet.sin_tetAngle₂_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.IdealTet.sin_tetAngle₂_eq","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/IdealTetLawOfSines.lean#L128-L134","doc":"The same, in the product form the derivative computation actually consumes:\n`sin θ₂ = ‖z‖ · sin θ₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.IdealTet.norm_eq_sin_div_sin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.IdealTet.norm_eq_sin_div_sin","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/IdealTetLawOfSines.lean#L107-L126","doc":"**THE LAW OF SINES FOR AN IDEAL TETRAHEDRON.**\n\nFor `Im z > 0`,\n\n    `‖z‖ = sin θ₂ / sin θ₃`\n\nwith `θ₂ = arg(1/(1−z))`, `θ₃ = arg(1 − 1/z)`.\n\nThis is what makes the radial reduction of Kummer's identity work: along a ray of\nconstant `arg z`, it is exactly the condition under which the Λ-side and the\ndilogarithm side have the same derivative. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:ideal-tetrahedron-law-of-sines","label":"thm:ideal-tetrahedron-law-of-sines","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ideal-tetrahedron-law-of-sines.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.IdealTet.sin_tetAngle₃_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.IdealTet.sin_tetAngle₃_pos","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/IdealTetLawOfSines.lean#L100-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.IdealTet.sin_tetAngle₂_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.IdealTet.sin_tetAngle₂_pos","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/IdealTetLawOfSines.lean#L96-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.IdealTet.sin_tetAngle₃","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.IdealTet.sin_tetAngle₃","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/IdealTetLawOfSines.lean#L75-L92","doc":"`sin θ₃ = Im z / (‖z‖ · ‖1 − z‖)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.IdealTet.sin_tetAngle₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.IdealTet.sin_tetAngle₂","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/IdealTetLawOfSines.lean#L64-L73","doc":"`sin θ₂ = Im z / ‖1 − z‖`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.IdealTet.ne_zero_of_im_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.IdealTet.ne_zero_of_im_pos","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/IdealTetLawOfSines.lean#L58-L60","doc":"On the upper half plane, `z ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.IdealTet.one_sub_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.IdealTet.one_sub_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/IdealTetLawOfSines.lean#L52-L56","doc":"On the upper half plane, `1 − z ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}